{
  "table_id": "Table_S22",
  "display_number": "S22",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S22. CHARLS-adapted PhenoAge validation against all-cause mortality.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [
    "Apparent mortality discrimination of the stored CHARLS-adapted score was evaluated in the archived analytical-cohort frame at a 7-year horizon. Mortality status and survival time were linked from Harmonized CHARLS D (waves 1–4, 2011–2018) and the CHARLS 2020 Exit Module. The score with chronological age yielded C = 0.746; age alone also yielded C = 0.746, whereas BAA alone yielded C = 0.502. Thus BAA added less than 0.001 to discrimination beyond age. The calibration slope was 2.17 and the scaled Brier score was 0.015; 202 deaths (6.2%) were recorded. These results do not establish equivalence to standard PhenoAge or validate the primary environmental association estimates. The stronger age-adjusted mortality association in Table S25 concerns a separately recalibrated score in a larger biomarker-eligible dataset; it does not externally validate or reconstruct the stored primary outcome."
  ],
  "notes_after": [
    "C-statistics computed via Harrell’s concordance from Cox proportional hazards models. Calibration assessed at 7.0-year prediction horizon. Scaled Brier score: 1 = perfect prediction, 0 = null model. Mortality follow-up: 2011–2020. The documented biomarker mapping is listed in Supplementary Table S19, but its implementation in the stored primary score could not be verified. BAA, biological age acceleration."
  ],
